WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
Put a newborn baby's
brain on a set of scales.

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.610
Weigh it again a few years later.

3
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.580
Now it's about three times as heavy.

4
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.830
Here's the twist.

5
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.200
A newborn has almost
all its neurons already.

6
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.160
So if it isn't making
lots of new nerve cells,

7
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.550
what's adding all that weight?

8
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.320
In this mission, you'll see the
brain begin as a simple tube,

9
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.550
which swells into three
parts: the forebrain,

10
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.760
midbrain and hindbrain.

11
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:32.390
And you'll zoom right in on neurons:
nerve cells that carry signals around the

12
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:33.410
brain.

13
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.560
Your mission: work out why a
baby's brain triples in weight.
